      "message": "Optional: this could be a type switch:\n\n    switch x :\u003d comp.(type) {\n        case SdkLibraryComponentDependency:\n           implicitSdkLib \u003d x.OptionalImplicitSdkLibrary()\n        case interface{ ProvidesUsesLib() *string }:\n           implicitSdkLib \u003d x.ProvidesUsesLib()\n    }\n\nIt\u0027s usually better to use a named interface instead of the anonymous interface, that allows adding compile time type assertions for the types that should implement the interface.\n\nAlso, is there any reason the SdkLibraryComponentDependency can\u0027t export ProvidesUsesLib() so there is a single interface to get this information?",
